<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds start mixed, short end weaker.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds start mixed, short end weaker.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 0750 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>* DUTCH STATE LOANS	 PRICES			  BID YIELDS</p>
<p>  June 1999 7.50 pct	106.30/40 (-0.03)	   3.91 (+0.04)</p>
<p>  Feb  2002		   114.49/59 (-0.02)	   4.62 (+0.02)</p>
<p>  Feb  2007 5.75 pct	101.95/03 (+0.04)	   5.48 (UNCHD)</p>
<p>  Jan  2023		   116.87/07 (+0.06)	   6.17 (UNCHD)</p>
<p>* BUND FUTURE (Sept)	103.02 (-0.01)</p>
<p>  TREASURIES  (Sept)	116.72 (+0.25 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>* DM/NLG			1.1263 (prev 1.1263)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 -0.01	LEVEL	  10-2 yr  157     (161)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.03	-0.05	  10-5 yr   88	(88)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.05	-0.04</p>
<p>---------------------------(Aug 1)------------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch longer bonds start firmer, recouping some of Thurs losses,  tracking Bunds in wake of firmer Treasuries close.</p>
<p>* But shorter paper weaker in slow trade, flattening curve. This trend  seen continuing as investors extend duration.</p>
<p>* U.S. July non-farm payrolls at 1230 GMT the main focus.</p>
